<title>USA: ComEd sees Ill. nuke on line Fri morning.</title>
<headline>ComEd sees Ill. nuke on line Fri morning.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's 789 megawatt Quad Cities nuclear power unit 2 in Cordova, Ill., shut Thursday for repairs, is expected to reconnect to the electricity grid Friday morning, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're at 20 percent power, and we're bringing it on-line this morning,&quot; said company spokesman Gary Wald.</p>
<p>The unit was taken off-line on Thursday due to a problem with a steam turbine valve, Wald said.</p>
<p>Commonwealth Edison is a unit of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
